<description>&lt;p&gt;Ukrainian naval drones have struck two Russian vessels at Libya's Benghazi port and off its coast, sinking one warship and damaging another, which Ukraine says was self-defence. Haftar, the eastern Libya leader, visited Erdogan in Turkey as ties between them thaw, while Russian forces later struck targets in Ukraine, killing two. Libyan forces continue shelling Haftar positions, and an armed group blocked the Hamada oil pipeline for over 20 days, causing $31 million in losses for the National Oil Corporation. The conflict recorded 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c6wy93q5wwqvo?at_medium=RSS&amp;amp;at_campaign=rss&quot;&gt;BBC News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/25/world/middleeast/libya-ukraine-russia-haftar.html&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxOTFNHOGZhYVZzNU52QmxZRktpTDIxSGliLXRkTGdLZk9IUTd2SmhZcGxzRUUtck8wRVZOZHBmWkxJRzNLY3lDOGIxOUFHX3VHR1dtZnVjRVV1ZFdmbXBGRUdBbzZQYV9LNUZ6aHJod2t6QWJvZTFVU05XT1RwODRiTXR1ZEJkQlJMU3QzNG9wbXJKeDZaQkFNNG53bVhYQmpxQ3NwV3Bnc0xZYjJXbG4ydGlR?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirAFBVV95cUxOTzIzWjZLTEdiVXRtR0I1cEJ3MFVCUzF5ZktKdWRUQlNtMEVDTnQ4Mk5xU2tvODVlRUJFeE5KOGlieGxsYkp5c1dhZklONzRZNW1VWTR4OVM1MGFQM0cxRXBaQm93b1lhWG1qR3F0ZGV2VTRRRGxtbTRkU1VYQ2c2dEtHckpXQmJCbmpYZlNKeFVrNW8zVjBldDFEWGc1TmIzRTJTM0ozNy1yanVq?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/23/world/europe/ukraine-libya-russian-ships.html&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eur